 "notes": "Observed 95% CL upper limit on the dilaton-like photon coupling |d_e| vs scalar DM mass m_phi from Fig. 4 of Van Tilburg et al. 2015 (dysprosium atomic spectroscopy). Extracted from the vector figure PlotdeLimTotal.pdf in the arXiv e-print: the thick observed-limit curves for the LT (2010-2012, red, path 19) and ST (19 Oct 2012, blue, path 28) datasets, combined as the lower envelope over their overlap and clipped to the plot frame (m_phi 1e-24 to ~8e-16 eV). Axis calibration from major tick strokes (x: log10 m_phi/eV, ticks -24,-22,-20,-18,-16; y: log10 d_e, ticks 0,-2,-4,-6,-8), cross-checked against the paper-quoted d_e~4.2e-8 at m_phi~1e-22 eV (extracted minimum 4.1e-8 at ~6e-23 eV). Bump near 7e-21 eV is the genuine sensitivity gap between the two datasets. Limit assumes phi is all of the DM at rho_DM=0.3 GeV/cm^3 (Eq.3); per task card, DM-search limits are reported at the paper native density and not rescaled. Canonical ScalarPhoton variable d_e (Damour-Donoghue) as defined in Eq.1 of the paper, identical to the task-card convention.",
